     "text": "{\"cost\": 8, \"rationale\": \"With no defences, every patched, segmented and mfa constant is false. A shortest path is: (1) phish_workstation, which gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; (2) pivot_internal, which gives reach_internal because segmented is false; (3) auth_ciserver, which gives foothold_ciserver; (4) escalate_ciserver, which gives admin_ciserver because patched_ciserver is false; (5) leak_secrets_ciserver, which gives stolen_dbadmin; (6) auth_db, which gives foothold_db; (7) escalate_db, which gives admin_db using stolen_dbadmin; (8) exfiltrate_db, which sets exfiltrated. No shorter path exists. Every exfiltrate step needs admin on db, fileserver or backup, which takes auth, escalate and exfiltrate (3 steps) and needs stolen_dbadmin plus reach_internal. The cheapest source of stolen_dbadmin is auth, escalate and leak on ciserver (3 steps), since the DC/ADFS route also needs kerberoast first. That route needs reach_internal and stolen_user, which phish plus pivot provide in 2 steps. Total: 2 + 3 + 3 = 8.\"}"
